window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7a5e03044e16c67c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"service-accounts\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">服务账户</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>服务账户让你可以在整个组织中运行和扩展无界面 Codex 工作流，而不必依赖某位员工的账户。每个持续集成（CI）运行器、定时任务或共享集成都有自己的 ChatGPT 工作区身份，并可像员工一样配置群组、角色、访问控制和审计能力。</p> <p>只有工作区所有者和管理员可以创建服务账户。他们可以允许其他人员或群组管理账户、配置插件或创建访问令牌。</p> <p>服务账户仅适用于按用量付费的套餐。</p> <p>服务账户代表一种非人工工作区身份；<a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">个人访问令牌</a>代表创建该令牌的工作区成员。API Platform 项目服务账户和 API 密钥使用独立的项目访问控制与计费方式。</p> <p><a id=\"create-and-set-up-a-service-account\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">创建并设置服务账户</h2> <p>下面的交互式演示以 GitHub 为例，展示如何创建账户、配置插件、创建令牌，以及分配群组和角色。</p> <p class=\"notice\">原网页此处包含交互演示，请通过“查看官方来源”联网查看。</p> <ol> <li>在工作区设置中打开<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/service-accounts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">服务账户（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>选择加号（<strong>+</strong>）按钮并输入描述性名称，例如 <code>release-automation</code>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Create</strong>（创建）。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"connect-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">连接插件</h2> <p>应直接为服务账户本身配置插件。它不会继承创建者的插件或已连接应用。</p> <ol> <li>打开该账户的 <strong>Plugins</strong>（插件）版块并选择 <strong>Add plugin</strong>（添加插件）。</li> <li>选择一个插件，并确认其显示为已配置或已启用。</li> </ol> <p><strong>Configure</strong> 和 <strong>Manager</strong> 角色可以配置插件；<strong>User</strong> 角色不可以。</p> <p><a id=\"create-an-access-token\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">创建访问令牌</h2> <p>在服务账户详情页中创建令牌。令牌代表服务账户，而不是创建令牌的人。</p> <ol> <li>打开账户，在 <strong>Access tokens</strong>（访问令牌）中选择 <strong>Create token</strong>（创建令牌）。</li> <li>为令牌命名，确认 <strong>Codex</strong> 范围并选择有效期。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Create</strong> 并将令牌保存到你的密钥管理器中。</li> </ol> <p>完整令牌只会显示一次。工作区策略会决定可选的有效期。</p> <p><a id=\"assign-roles-and-groups\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">分配角色和群组</h2> <p>服务账户可以像人工工作区成员一样获得工作区角色并加入群组。请直接为服务账户分配访问权限；它不会继承创建者的权限。</p> <p>若要允许人员或群组管理该账户，请选择 <strong>Share</strong>（共享），再选择 <strong>Add people or groups</strong>（添加人员或群组），然后分配角色：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>共享账户角色</th> <th>配置账户和其插件</th> <th>创建服务账户访问令牌</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>User</strong></td> <td>否</td> <td>是</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Configure</strong></td> <td>是</td> <td>否</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Manager</strong></td> <td>是</td> <td>是</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>这些角色适用于管理服务账户的人员，与分配给服务账户本身的工作区角色和群组相互独立。</p> <p><strong>Configure</strong> 和 <strong>Manager</strong> 可以启用或停用账户。只有工作区所有者和管理员可以创建、删除或共享账户。操作人员使用自己的 ChatGPT 账户登录后管理共享账户。</p> <p>有关工作区权限的更多信息，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"run-codex-without-signing-in\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">无需登录即可运行 Codex</h2> <p>服务账户访问令牌要求 Codex CLI 版本为 <code>0.142.0</code> 或更高版本。设置 <code>CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN</code> 后即可运行 Codex，无需打开浏览器：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">export CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN=\"&lt;service-account-access-token&gt;\"\ncodex exec --json \"Inspect this repository and summarize its current state.\"\n</code></pre> <p>在 CI 环境中，请通过密钥管理器或运行器密钥提供令牌。</p> <p>在受信任的计算机上保存登录凭据时，可通过标准输入传递令牌：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">printf '%s' \"$CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN\" | codex login --with-access-token\ncodex exec \"Summarize the changes in the current branch.\"\n</code></pre> <p>这会在本地保存凭据。在共享或临时运行器上，请使用 <code>CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN</code>，不要保存登录状态。</p> <p><a id=\"provision-service-accounts-with-scim\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"scim\">使用 SCIM 配置服务账户</h2> <p>如果你的工作区支持通过跨域身份管理系统（SCIM）协议配置服务账户，请在身份提供商中将 <code>userType</code> 设为 <code>ServiceAccount</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"schemas\": [\"urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:User\"],\n  \"userName\": \"svc-codex-release@company.example\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Codex release automation\",\n  \"active\": true,\n  \"userType\": \"ServiceAccount\"\n}\n</code></pre> <p>将该身份分配到工作区和所需群组，然后同步。身份提供商负责管理账户名称、群组成员资格和生命周期。由 SCIM 管理的账户不能在 ChatGPT 中重命名或删除。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与配置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-service-accounts-with-the-admin-api\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"admin-api\">使用 Admin API 管理服务账户</h2> <p>如果你的工作区具有访问权限，可以使用 ChatGPT Admin API 密钥管理账户、令牌和共享设置。读取操作需要 <code>chatgpt.enterprise.service_account.read</code> 权限；更改操作需要 <code>chatgpt.enterprise.service_account.write</code> 权限。服务账户令牌不能用于对 Admin API 请求进行身份验证。</p> <p>可用操作和当前请求路径请参阅 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"accounts\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">账户</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>操作</th> <th>方法</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>列出账户</td> <td><code>GET</code></td> <td>返回工作区服务账户</td> </tr> <tr> <td>创建账户</td> <td><code>POST</code></td> <td>创建一个命名的服务账户</td> </tr> <tr> <td>获取账户</td> <td><code>GET</code></td> <td>返回一个服务账户</td> </tr> <tr> <td>启用或停用账户</td> <td><code>PATCH</code></td> <td>更新账户的 <code>enabled</code> 值</td> </tr> <tr> <td>删除账户</td> <td><code>DELETE</code></td> <td>移除账户并撤销其令牌</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>使用 <code>POST /v1/manage/workspaces/{workspace_id}/service-accounts</code> 创建账户。账户更新只会更改 <code>enabled</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"tokens\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">令牌</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>操作</th> <th>方法</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>列出令牌</td> <td><code>GET</code></td> <td>返回账户的令牌元数据</td> </tr> <tr> <td>创建令牌</td> <td><code>POST</code></td> <td>创建限定范围的访问令牌</td> </tr> <tr> <td>撤销令牌</td> <td><code>DELETE</code></td> <td>永久撤销一个令牌</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>例如，创建一个 30 天后过期的 Codex 令牌：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"name\": \"production-release-runner\",\n  \"ttl\": 2592000,\n  \"scopes\": [\"chatgpt.workspace.feature.allow-codex-local-access.access\"]\n}\n</code></pre> <p><code>ttl</code> 是以秒为单位的令牌有效期。有限有效期必须短于一年，并遵循工作区的有效期策略。完整的 <code>access_token</code> 仅在创建时返回。</p> <p>Admin API 还可以列出、添加、更新和移除共享账户的访问权限。其角色值为 <code>manager</code>、<code>configurer</code> 和 <code>user</code>；其中 <code>configurer</code> 在 ChatGPT 界面中显示为 <strong>Configure</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"secure-and-manage-service-accounts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">安全地管理服务账户</h2> <ul> <li>只授予工作流所需的角色、群组、插件和连接。</li> <li>将令牌存储在密钥管理器中，并使用受信任的运行器。</li> <li>不要将凭据写入日志、聊天消息或源代码管理。</li> <li>设置有限的有效期，并定期检查账户访问权限和活动。</li> <li>轮换令牌时，先创建替代令牌、更新工作流并验证访问，再在工作区或 Admin API 中撤销旧令牌。</li> <li>如果令牌泄露，请立即撤销，并调查该账户近期的活动。</li> <li>在工作区或 Admin API 中停用或删除不再使用的账户。这两种操作都会撤销所有活动令牌。停用的账户可以重新启用，但需要使用新令牌；删除操作无法撤销。</li> </ul> <p>运行记录会归属于服务账户。可用的工作区分析与审计记录也可能显示是谁创建了令牌或更改了账户设置。请在 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>中确认具体事件覆盖范围。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">个人访问令牌</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与配置</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64\">治理</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API 与审计事件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">非交互模式</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"service-accounts\">Service accounts</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Service accounts let you run and scale headless Codex workflows across your organization without relying on an employee's account. Each continuous integration (CI) runner, scheduled job, or shared integration gets its own ChatGPT workspace identity, with the same groups, roles, access controls, and auditability you expect for people.</p> <p>Only workspace owners and admins can create service accounts. They can let other people or groups manage an account, configure plugins, or create access tokens.</p> <p>Service accounts are available only on pay-as-you-go plans.</p> <p>A service account represents a non-human workspace identity. A <a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">personal access token</a> represents the workspace member who creates it. API Platform project service accounts and API keys use separate project access and billing.</p> <h2 id=\"create-and-set-up-a-service-account\">Create and set up a service account</h2> <p>This interactive walkthrough uses GitHub as an example: create an account, configure a plugin, create a token, and assign groups and roles.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/service-accounts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Service accounts (online)</a> in your workspace settings.</li> <li>Select the plus (<strong>+</strong>) button and enter a descriptive name, such as <code>release-automation</code>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Create</strong>.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"connect-a-plugin\">Connect a plugin</h2> <p>Configure plugins for the service account itself. It doesn't inherit the creator's plugins or connected apps.</p> <ol> <li>Open the account's <strong>Plugins</strong> section and select <strong>Add plugin</strong>.</li> <li>Choose a plugin and confirm that it shows as configured or enabled.</li> </ol> <p>The <strong>Configure</strong> and <strong>Manager</strong> roles can set up plugins. The <strong>User</strong> role can't.</p> <h2 id=\"create-an-access-token\">Create an access token</h2> <p>Create a token from the service account's detail page. The token represents the service account, not the person who creates it.</p> <ol> <li>Open the account and select <strong>Create token</strong> in <strong>Access tokens</strong>.</li> <li>Name the token, confirm the <strong>Codex</strong> scope, and choose an expiration.</li> <li>Select <strong>Create</strong> and save the token in your secret manager.</li> </ol> <p>The full token appears only once. Workspace policies control which expirations are available.</p> <h2 id=\"assign-roles-and-groups\">Assign roles and groups</h2> <p>A service account can receive workspace roles and join groups like a human workspace member. Assign its access directly; it doesn't inherit the creator's permissions.</p> <p>To let people or groups manage the account, select <strong>Share</strong>, then <strong>Add people or groups</strong>, and assign a role:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Shared-account role</th> <th>Configure the account and its plugins</th> <th>Create service-account access tokens</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>User</strong></td> <td>No</td> <td>Yes</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Configure</strong></td> <td>Yes</td> <td>No</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Manager</strong></td> <td>Yes</td> <td>Yes</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>These roles apply to people managing the account. They are separate from the workspace roles and groups assigned to the service account.</p> <p><strong>Configure</strong> and <strong>Manager</strong> can enable or disable the account. Only workspace owners and admins can create, delete, or share accounts. Operators manage shared accounts while signed in to their own ChatGPT accounts.</p> <p>For more about workspace permissions, see <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"run-codex-without-signing-in\">Run Codex without signing in</h2> <p>Service-account access tokens require Codex CLI version <code>0.142.0</code> or later. Set <code>CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN</code> and run Codex without opening a browser:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">export CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN=\"&lt;service-account-access-token&gt;\"\ncodex exec --json \"Inspect this repository and summarize its current state.\"\n</code></pre> <p>In CI, provide the token through a secret manager or runner secret.</p> <p>To save a login on a trusted machine, pass the token through standard input:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">printf '%s' \"$CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN\" | codex login --with-access-token\ncodex exec \"Summarize the changes in the current branch.\"\n</code></pre> <p>This saves the credential locally. On shared or temporary runners, use <code>CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN</code> without saving a login.</p> <h2 id=\"provision-service-accounts-with-scim\">Provision service accounts with SCIM</h2> <p>If your workspace supports service-account provisioning through the System for Cross-domain Identity Management (SCIM) protocol, set <code>userType</code> to <code>ServiceAccount</code> in your identity provider:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"schemas\": [\"urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:User\"],\n  \"userName\": \"svc-codex-release@company.example\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Codex release automation\",\n  \"active\": true,\n  \"userType\": \"ServiceAccount\"\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Assign the identity to the workspace and required groups, then sync it. The identity provider manages the account's name, group membership, and lifecycle. SCIM-managed accounts can't be renamed or deleted in ChatGPT. See <a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-service-accounts-with-the-admin-api\">Manage service accounts with the Admin API</h2> <p>If your workspace has access, use a ChatGPT Admin API key to manage accounts, tokens, and sharing. Read operations require <code>chatgpt.enterprise.service_account.read</code>; changes require <code>chatgpt.enterprise.service_account.write</code>. A service-account token can't authenticate Admin API requests.</p> <p>Check the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a> for available operations and current request paths.</p> <h3 id=\"accounts\">Accounts</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Operation</th> <th>Method</th> <th>What it does</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>List accounts</td> <td><code>GET</code></td> <td>Returns workspace service accounts</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Create an account</td> <td><code>POST</code></td> <td>Creates a named service account</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Get an account</td> <td><code>GET</code></td> <td>Returns one service account</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Enable or disable an account</td> <td><code>PATCH</code></td> <td>Updates the account's <code>enabled</code> value</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Delete an account</td> <td><code>DELETE</code></td> <td>Removes the account and revokes its tokens</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Create accounts with <code>POST /v1/manage/workspaces/{workspace_id}/service-accounts</code>. Account updates change only <code>enabled</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"tokens\">Tokens</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Operation</th> <th>Method</th> <th>What it does</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>List tokens</td> <td><code>GET</code></td> <td>Returns the account's token metadata</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Create a token</td> <td><code>POST</code></td> <td>Creates a scoped access token</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Revoke a token</td> <td><code>DELETE</code></td> <td>Permanently revokes one token</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For example, create a Codex token that expires after 30 days:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-json\">{\n  \"name\": \"production-release-runner\",\n  \"ttl\": 2592000,\n  \"scopes\": [\"chatgpt.workspace.feature.allow-codex-local-access.access\"]\n}\n</code></pre> <p><code>ttl</code> is the token lifetime in seconds. A finite lifetime must be less than one year and follow your workspace's expiration policy. The full <code>access_token</code> is returned only when the token is created.</p> <p>The Admin API can also list, add, update, and remove shared-account access. Its role values are <code>manager</code>, <code>configurer</code>, and <code>user</code>; <code>configurer</code> appears as <strong>Configure</strong> in ChatGPT.</p> <h2 id=\"secure-and-manage-service-accounts\">Secure and manage service accounts</h2> <ul> <li>Grant only the roles, groups, plugins, and connections the workflow needs.</li> <li>Store tokens in a secret manager and use trusted runners.</li> <li>Keep credentials out of logs, chat messages, and source control.</li> <li>Set finite expirations and review account access and activity regularly.</li> <li>Rotate a token by creating a replacement, updating the workflow, verifying access, and revoking the old token in the workspace or Admin API.</li> <li>Revoke exposed tokens immediately and investigate the account's recent activity.</li> <li>Disable or delete unused accounts in the workspace or Admin API. Both actions revoke all active tokens. Disabled accounts can be re-enabled with new tokens; deletion can't be undone.</li> </ul> <p>Runs are attributed to the service account. Available workspace analytics and audit records can also identify who created tokens or changed account settings. Confirm event coverage in the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">Personal access tokens</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64\">Governance</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API and audit events</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">Non-interactive mode</a></li> </ul>"};
